        "Content": "Ballyshannon Lodge is a charming and distinguished country residence set on approximately 9 acres of high-quality land, complete with 6 loose boxes, tennis court, and extensive outbuildings. Accessed via electric gates off Ballyshannon Road, the property offers privacy, maturity, and exceptional potential for equestrian or lifestyle use.\r\n\r\nExtending to approximately 310 sq. m., the residence provides well-balanced accommodation, enhanced by many original features throughout.\r\n\r\nBallyshannon Lodge is a unique and impressive residence, combining period charm with substantial accommodation and exceptional outdoor facilities. Its setting, scale, and equestrian potential make it a standout lifestyle opportunity.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Ground Floor\r\n\r\n•\tEntrance Hall\r\n        A welcoming space featuring a hardwood front door, stained glass windows, and original staircase. \r\n•\tDining Room (5.7 x 4.28)\r\n        Carpeted flooring, feature fireplace, and ceiling coving. \r\n•\tSitting Room (5.7 x 4.26)\r\n        Carpeted flooring, ceiling rose, feature fireplace with tiled inset. \r\n•\tKitchen (4.6 x 5.5)\r\n        Tiled floor, fitted with hardwood kitchen units and an oil-fired Aga range set within a brick surround.\r\n        French doors open onto the patio area. \r\n•\tStudy / Office (4.42 x 4.9)\r\n        Bright and spacious with parquet flooring, wood panelling, and a solid fuel stove with back boiler. \r\n•\tFamily Room (Long Room) (7.4 x 4.2)\r\n        A warm and inviting space with solid oak flooring and a feature fireplace with stove. \r\n•\tAdditional Areas\r\n        Storeroom (2.6 x 1.3), rear hallway with access to patio, guest W.C., and storage cupboard (3.3 x 1.1). \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t          \r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\n•\tLanding Area with guest W.C. (2 x 1.15) and shower room (2 x 2.8) with Triton electric shower. \r\n•\tMaster Bedroom (5.3 x 4.3)\r\n        Spacious and overlooking the landscaped gardens. \r\n•\tEn-Suite (3.7 x 2.7)\r\n        Fully tiled with sunken bath, power shower, and dual sinks. \r\n•\tDressing Room / Bedroom (4.9 x 4.97) \r\n•\tBedroom 2 (5.8 x 4.3)\r\n        Large double room with cast iron fireplace. \r\n•\tBedroom 3 (3.2 x 1.96) \r\n•\tBedroom 4 (2.7 x 4.7)"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Outdoor & Equestrian Features\r\n•\tAccess via electric gates onto a private driveway \r\n•\tManicured lawns with mature hedging and shrubs \r\n•\tAmple parking to the rear with double garage \r\n•\tEnclosed tennis court \r\n•\tStable block with 6 loose boxes, including a foaling stable \r\n\r\nLocation\r\n•\tJust off the M9 motorway \r\n•\tApproximately 40 km from Dublin \r\n•\tOnly 7 km from Kilcullen \r\n•\tLocated in the heart of a renowned bloodstock region \r\n•\tClose to excellent primary schools in Ballyshannon and Cutbush \r\n\r\n•\tEnclosed yard with independent access onto Cutbush Road \r\n•\tTwo storage / machinery sheds \r\n•\tHigh-quality land laid out in one division, currently under grass with stud rail fencing \r\n\r\nThis property is ideally suited to an equestrian enterprise or hobby farm."
      },
      {
